;; stdlib/ecowar/biome_mod.prn — real per-biome gameplay modifiers (EMILY/BACKLOG.md SECTION 382).
;; Founder shared a 4-biome map design (Verdant Wilds/jungle, Ash Barrens/high-risk-decay, Frozen
;; Reach/defensive, Blighted Grid/chaos) and asked for critique before building -- see
;; ECOWAR/docs/NORTHSTAR_BIOMES.md for the full critique (renamed away from the reference design's
;; own Minecraft-specific "Pillager"/"Dragon" terminology, which has no real connection to
;; ECOWAR's own established vocabulary).
;;
;; Real, pure PARENA logic -- no #target/inline-c needed at all, same "real decision rule, no FFI
;; escape" shape ecowar/allcap_mod.prn already established. Biome ids match HexBiome
;; (packages/livingmap/hex_grid.h): 0=Verdant Wilds, 1=Ash Barrens, 2=Frozen Reach,
;; 3=Blighted Grid.
;;
;; on-biome-convert-resistance-multiplier-pct: real, named numbers for "villages flip often"
;; (Verdant Wilds, founder's own reference design) and "cells stabilize longer"/"structures harder
;; to destroy" (Frozen Reach) -- the two biomes whose own described mechanics map directly onto
;; the ALREADY-BUILT town convert-resistance system (town.c's town_attempt_convert already reads
;; a per-town-type resistance from frontier_village_mod.prn/walled_hamlet_mod.prn; this multiplies
;; that real value by the town's own real biome). Ash Barrens and Blighted Grid return the neutral
;; 100 here -- their own real mechanics (faster corruption growth, the corruption-driven neutral-
;; cell flip) are handled by hex_grid_tick_corruption (hex_grid.c) instead, not resistance at all.

(module ecowar/biome-mod)
(export on-biome-convert-resistance-multiplier-pct)

(defn on-biome-convert-resistance-multiplier-pct [(biome : I32)] : I32
  (if (= biome 0) 70   ;; Verdant Wilds -- "villages flip often": 30% easier to convert
    (if (= biome 2) 140  ;; Frozen Reach -- "cells stabilize longer": 40% harder to convert
      100)))              ;; Ash Barrens / Blighted Grid -- neutral here, see this file's own header comment
